# The main menu's cutscene: your own character - dressed and coloured as the
# wardrobe has it - talking with Bryn. Every character is a stack of close-up
# layers, one per item, drawn in any colours; the commands are described in
# src/main/java/com/larsons/game/cutscene/Cutscene.java and assets/cutscenes/README.md.

actor you  "You"  player
actor bryn "Bryn" body=feminine shirt=laced_shirt ears=elven nose=button eyes=ice_blue eyebrows=soft mouth=wide hair=side_part colour.body=#d9a074 colour.hair=platinum colour.shirt=royal_blue colour.eyes=emerald

stand you left
stand bryn right
wait 1.2
say bryn "Hey! You look different today."
say you laugh "Same me. New palette."
say bryn surprise "Wait... the colours aren't painted on?"
say you explain "Every pixel of me is a label, not a colour. The game looks the colour up as it draws me."
colour you hair #3b7fe8 1.2
say you "So my hair can be blue..."
colour you hair #e2588f 1.2
say you "...or pink, without redrawing a single frame."
clip bryn laugh 2.0
wait 1.8
say bryn explain "And every layer is its own sprite: hair, eyes, shirt, ears. Swap any of them."
wear bryn hair pixie
colour bryn hair #f2c14e 0.8
say bryn "That's how a cutscene can star anyone. Even you, just as you made yourself."
tint all #ffb070 0.35 1.5
say you "Warm light for the good news..."
tint all #5a78ff 0.45 1.2
say bryn surprise "...and cold for the bad!"
tint all none 1.0
flash you #ffffff 0.5
say you laugh "Let's stick to good news."
colour you hair reset 1.0
wear bryn hair side_part
colour bryn hair platinum 0.8
wait 2.5
loop
